            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One familiar addressee as object is त्वाम् (tvām). The speaker plus one other is आवाम् (āvām). Turn the dual toward two addressees."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: युवाम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "युवाम् (yuvām) means “you two” as the object."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सः युवाम् पश्यति। saḥ yuvām paśyati. He sees you two."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Whitney §491 lists युवाम् (yuvām) beside आवाम् (āvām). Both are independent dual forms; the opening tells you whether the pair includes the speaker or consists of the two people addressed."
            }
